# Every service's Dockerfile builds with `context: .` (repo root) so libs/shared can
# be COPYed alongside each services/<name>/ — without this file, every `docker build`
# re-sends the entire repo (every service's own .venv, ui-react's node_modules, .git)
# as build context, multiplied by however many images are being built. None of these
# are ever COPYed into an image (Dockerfiles copy specific src/pyproject.toml/settings.yaml
# paths only; scenarios/ is bind-mounted read-only at runtime, never baked in).

.git/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/htmlcov/
**/coverage.xml
**/coverage.json
**/.coverage
scenarios/**/data/
scenarios/**/model/
infra/postgres/data/
infra/qdrant/storage/
infra/minio/data/
infra/logto/data/
